{"id":1942,"slug":"the-docks-of-new-york","title":"The Docks of New York","year":1928,"country":"United States","duration":75,"spine":531,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/1942-the-docks-of-new-york","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/c95ef17d3f5b91ddf79776a8ae82423d/5CUoTbddFmMGGKxJr3F6e9FZpX9Nor_large.jpg","description":"\nRoughneck stoker Bill Roberts (George Bancroft) gets into all sorts of trouble during a brief shore leave when he falls hard for Mae (Betty Compson), a wise and weary dance-hall girl, in Josef von Sternberg’s evocative portrait of working-class waterfront folk. Fog-enshrouded cinematography by Harold Rosson (Sunset Boulevard), and sensual performances by Bancroft and Compson make this one of the legendary director’s finest works, and one of the most exquisitely crafted films of the era.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Josef von Sternberg","slug":"josef-von-sternberg"}],"cast":[{"actor":"George Bancroft","role":"The Stoker","slug":"george-bancroft"},{"actor":"Clyde Cook","role":"His pal","slug":"clyde-cook"},{"actor":"Betty Compson","role":"A girl","slug":"betty-compson"},{"actor":"Mitchell Lewis","role":"The third engineer","slug":"mitchell-lewis"},{"actor":"Olga Baclanova","role":"His wife","slug":"olga-baclanova"},{"actor":"Gustav von Seyffertitz","role":"Hymn-book Harry","slug":"gustav-von-seyffertitz"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Josef von Sternberg","slug":"josef-von-sternberg"},{"role":"Photographed by","person":"Harold Rosson","slug":null},{"role":"Story and screenplay by","person":"Jules Furthman","slug":null},{"role":"Suggested by","person":"John Monk Saunders's \"The Dock Walloper\"","slug":null},{"role":"Titles by","person":"Julian Johnson","slug":null},{"role":"Edited by","person":"Helen Lewis","slug":null}],"pickedBy":[],"related":[773,362,21766],"setFilms":[],"inSets":[1000744]}